WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.925
The first time, the chat has no model.

2
00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:06.673
The indicator shows it in red and you can only check the status.

3
00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.839
Open the settings with the gear icon.

4
00:00:10.439 --> 00:00:15.913
In the Model block, choose the provider: Google Gemini, local Ollama, OpenAI,

5
00:00:15.913 --> 00:00:18.259
or any OpenAI-compatible address.

6
00:00:18.259 --> 00:00:20.676
Picking one fills in the base URL.

7
00:00:22.276 --> 00:00:23.410
Paste the API key.

8
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.188
It is stored only on this computer, in your settings folder,

9
00:00:27.188 --> 00:00:28.952
and never in the repository.

10
00:00:28.952 --> 00:00:30.841
With Ollama it can stay empty.

11
00:00:32.441 --> 00:00:35.945
Enter the model that runs the conversation and builds the design.

12
00:00:35.945 --> 00:00:37.616
The reviewer model is optional:

13
00:00:37.616 --> 00:00:42.359
it reads each circuit before it is written and each board proposal before it is applied.

14
00:00:42.359 --> 00:00:45.000
Leave it empty to work without that second check.

15
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.613
Autorouting uses FreeRouting, which needs Java 17 or later.

16
00:00:50.613 --> 00:00:53.673
Press Detect Java, or type the path yourself.

17
00:00:55.273 --> 00:01:00.269
Turn autorouting on and set the fabrication minimums in millimetres: track width,

18
00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:03.476
clearance, via diameter and drill, and minimum hole.

19
00:01:03.476 --> 00:01:06.128
While it is off, the tool does not show up.

20
00:01:07.728 --> 00:01:08.063
Save.

21
00:01:08.063 --> 00:01:13.013
The settings stay on your computer and take precedence over any .env file.

22
00:01:14.613 --> 00:01:18.722
The model indicator turns green and the project shows autorouting as active.

23
00:01:18.722 --> 00:01:21.317
Autoroute now appears in the quick actions menu.

24
00:01:21.317 --> 00:01:23.750
You are ready to describe your first circuit.
